            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for rotten, then the Latin for a tavern hostess."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: querēla, querēlae",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "querēla, querēlae — \"a complaint\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hospitēs multās querēlās dē caupōne habent. The guests have many complaints about the innkeeper."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First declension, feminine: querēla, querēlae f., also spelled querella. English quarrel comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "querēla is built on queror 'to complain' with the suffix -ēla (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English quarrel comes from it through Old French."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
