              "text": "rapāx, rapācis — \"grasping, greedy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Caupō rapāx magnum pretium prō cēnā parvā rogat. The grasping innkeeper asks a big price for a small dinner."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An adjective of one ending: rapāx, genitive rapācis. Also of wild beasts: ravenous. English rapacious comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rapāx is built on rapiō 'to seize, to snatch' with the suffix -āx 'given to' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English rapacious comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
