            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In cubiculō sordēs sunt, et hospes īrātus est. There is dirt in the bedroom, and the guest is angry."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, feminine: sordēs, sordis f., mostly plural sordēs, sordium. English sordid comes from the adjective sordidus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sordēs is built on sordeō 'to be dirty' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English sordid comes from the related adjective sordidus."
            }
          ]
        },
